# Architecture B — Showcase execution runtime

## Goal

**Full execution transparency. Minimal research storage. Minimal disk writes. Minimal Railway resource usage.**

This is NOT "remove dashboard features." It IS "remove research infrastructure."

## Three roles

| Runtime | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| Research bot (`bybit-15m-research-bot`) | Collect everything, log everything, export everything |
| Showcase bot (Railway `btc_conservative_agent.py`) | Trade, mirror signals, display operator state — **no research warehouse** |
| NestJS API | Bitfinex copy execution, relay wake, subscriber lots |

## KEEP (execution visibility)

Account, positions, orders, signal pipeline, AI snapshot + last 5 decisions, system status (engine version, runtime mode, signal hash, parity/sync).

Dashboard lives in **bot.py full HTML** (pathway lab, toggles, trade tables). `showcase_ui.py` only blocks warehouse export routes and adds `/api/sync_status` + `/api/fresh_start`. Do not swap in the minimal mirror HTML unless explicitly requested.

## REMOVE on Railway (research-only)

Disable writes and CPU for: replay buffers, counterfactual studies, signal_snapshot/replay JSONL, CSV exports, ai_input_log, near_miss, shadow_reject, feature drift, research KPI refresh, analytics exports.

Gate with `_showcase_execution_only()` — set by `btc_conservative_agent.py` via `SHOWCASE_EXECUTION_ONLY=1`.

## ALLOW (small operational state)

`account_state.json`, `order_state.json`, `position_state.json`, in-memory `ai_history` (cap 5 on showcase).

## Patch survival

Research sync overwrites `bot.py`. All showcase gates MUST live in `scripts/patch-btc-bot-production.mjs` so they re-apply on every `npm run sync:btc-research-bot`.

## Rule of thumb

If needed to **operate, monitor, debug, or understand live execution** → keep visible.

If exists only for **analysis, training, replay, counterfactuals, or offline exports** → strip from Railway runtime.

Signal logic must stay **byte-for-byte parity** with research bot (`verify:signal-parity --full`).
